        <div class="article-header">
            <h1>Using Marketplaces to Internationalize Your Company</h1>
            <div class="meta-info">
                By <strong>Marcelo Cavalcante dos Santos</strong> | Published on January 28, 2026
            </div>
        </div>

        <img src="https://googleusercontent.com/image_generation_content/10" alt="International Marketplace Strategy" class="cover-image">

        <div class="content">
            <p>International expansion is no longer exclusive to large corporations. The advancement of global e-commerce, combined with modern logistics solutions and the efficient use of international marketplaces, now allows Brazilian small and medium-sized enterprises to access the U.S. market with speed, controlled risk, and strategic planning.</p>

            <h2>1. Phased Model: Test the Market with Lower Risk</h2>
            <p>The phased model is ideal for companies seeking to begin their international expansion cautiously. In this structure, the marketplace serves as a gateway, allowing products to be shipped directly from Brazil to the end customer in the United States. Lightweight, high value-added products perform particularly well under this model, as they offer strong margins and immediate acceptance.</p>

            <h2>2. Structured Model: Scale Through Advanced Logistics</h2>
            <p>The second path is designed for companies with greater investment capacity. Under this model, operations begin with the support of U.S.-based logistics partners, including warehousing services, fulfillment centers, and fast regional delivery networks. This infrastructure provides agility and immediate competitiveness.</p>

            <h2>Strategic Considerations</h2>
            <p>To transform either model into a consistent international expansion project, managers should follow several essential best practices. Legal and tax compliance in the United States must be carefully mapped, including accurate customs classification and the proper handling of revenue in U.S. dollars.</p>

            <p>Institutional initiatives such as those provided by <strong>ApexBrasil</strong> play a meaningful role in this process, offering training and technical guidance to Brazilian companies seeking secure access to the U.S. market.</p>

